# `this.lid = undefined` in the constructor gives every object the key, so that all have one shape, and fills nothing. Where the written type lets the field be left out and no maker goes on to fill it, the slot is a granule of the Extension
# that an object gets where something is stored. The key stays in the order of the birth: one order. `words` and `from` are filled by a second constructor, on which another maker builds: they lie in the cell. `price` is born with a value.
# `later` is stored on some of the objects: the layout has the word that names an Extension, whatever becomes of the others. A layout without it keeps its fields in the cell.
# -- source: left-undefined.ts
